course: dictionary
lesson: 13401
title: Heralded: a sign that something is coming
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Heralded is the past tense of herald. When one thing heralds another, it is a sign that the other thing is on its way. «Dark clouds heralded the storm.» The clouds came first, so we know the storm was coming.
explain: Heralded can also mean announced loudly or welcomed in public. «Trumpets heralded the arrival of the king.» The trumpets were loud, and they told everyone the king was here. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: Herald can also work as an adjective. «The much-heralded new game» means a game that people talked about with great excitement before it came out. Ask yourself: what came first, and what was the big news? Then swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense.
fact: Heralded is the past tense of the verb herald.
fact: «Heralded» means was a sign that something was coming.
fact: «Heralded» can also mean announced loudly or welcomed in public.
fact: «Much-heralded» means talked about with great excitement before it happened.
fact: In stories, trumpets often heralded the arrival of a king or queen.
exercise: «Dark clouds heralded the storm.» What does heralded mean here? | Was very quiet and calm | *Was a sign that the storm was coming | Stopped the storm from coming | Washed the storm away
exercise: «The new stadium was much-heralded before it opened.» What does much-heralded mean? | Very small and quiet | *Talked about with great excitement before it happened | Forgotten by everyone | Closed for repairs
exercise: Which word is a past tense form of herald in this sentence: «The rain heralded the spring.»? | the | spring | rain | *heralded
test: «The bells heralded the start of the festival.» What does heralded mean here? | Made the bells stop ringing | Muffled the sound of the festival | Forgot the start of the festival | *Was a sign that the festival was starting
test: Mum says the new film was much-heralded. What does she mean? | *It was talked about with great excitement before it came out | It is a very old film | It was cancelled before anyone saw it | It is a short film with no story
exam: «Red sky at night heralds fine weather.» What does heralds mean here? | It shouts loudly about the rain | It is a word for the colour of the sky | It makes the weather go away | *It is a sign that fine weather is coming
